## Slide 14 — Module 3: ML Distraction Detection Model

**Major rewrite needed — NO ML model is used:**

| # | Current (Wrong) | ✅ Correct |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | "Trains a binary classifier on BigQuery feature windows" | Wrong — FocusEcho uses a **deterministic rule-based engine**, not a trained ML model |
| 2 | "Google Cloud AI Platform / Vertex AI" | Not used |
| 3 | "scikit-learn (RandomForest + XGBoost)" | Not used |
| 4 | "BigQuery ML for in-warehouse baseline" | Not used |

**Correct Module 3 description:**
> FocusEcho uses a **custom Rule Engine** (`rule_engine.py`) that computes distraction risk using:
> - **App category weights** (always_distraction=60pts, allowed_with_limit=20pts, unknown=30pts)
> - **Time-away duration** (logarithmic penalty)
> - **Distraction frequency** (last 30 min count × 5pts)
> - **Recovery bonus** (−15pts if returned < 30s)
> - Final **risk labels**: SAFE / LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH / CRITICAL

---

## Slide 15 — Module 3: Technical Details / Algorithm

Replace pseudocode with **actual rule engine logic:**
```
INPUT: List of distraction events for session
OUTPUT: risk_label (SAFE/LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH/CRITICAL), focus_score (0-100)

1. Filter events from last 30 minutes
2. Get latest event: app_category, time_away_seconds, returned_to_origin
3. score = 0.0
4. score += category_weight[app_category]  
   # always_distraction=60, allowed_with_limit=20, unknown=30
5. score += (log(time_away_seconds+1) / log(60)) × 25
6. score += distraction_count_last_30min × 5
7. IF returned_to_focus AND time_away < 30s: score -= 15
8. score = clamp(score, 0, 100)
9. risk_label = CRITICAL(≥70) / HIGH(≥45) / MEDIUM(≥20) / LOW(<20)
10. focus_score = 100 - count_penalty - recovery_penalty - critical_penalty + time_bonus
```

